1
00:00:12,730 --> 00:00:15,550
♪I lean and gaze at misty waves afar♪

2
00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:18,320
♪Tears fall on the ancient road
'neath the setting sun♪

3
00:00:19,330 --> 00:00:21,460
♪One lone shadow on the cold river♪

4
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:23,910
♪In dreams, I return to the old window♪

5
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:28,670
♪Mountains stretch, the road home fades♪

6
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:32,030
♪A flute cries out, hooves hurry on♪

7
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:34,790
♪My heart adrift beneath a frosted moon♪

8
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:38,220
♪Drinking alone, I mourn our parting♪

9
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:40,050
♪Night turns cold, wind stirs the veil♪

10
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:41,760
♪Old robes recall forgotten days♪

11
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:43,570
♪Heart sore, a lone goose flies south♪

12
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:45,230
♪Where shall I send this letter?♪

13
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:47,760
♪Lost in thought through endless nights♪

14
00:00:47,770 --> 00:00:49,000
♪Love runs deep, dreams linger on♪

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,390
♪Only sorrow remains♪

16
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:53,340
♪A cup of wine, my shadow makes us two♪

17
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:54,980
♪Drunk and lost through flashing blades♪

18
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:56,870
♪I curse how swiftly the years pass by♪

19
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:58,580
♪The wandering road goes on♪

20
00:00:58,590 --> 00:01:01,020
♪Desolate, time frosts my youthful hair♪

21
00:01:01,030 --> 00:01:02,340
♪Through the years, love still burns♪

22
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:04,530
♪A thousand tears fall♪

23
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:08,030
♪Worlds apart, tears stain my sleeves♪

24
00:01:08,150 --> 00:01:11,300
♪Old dreams haunt my heart,
tears cloud my eyes♪

25
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:13,340
♪Heartbroken, soul-worn,
pain won't fade♪

26
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:14,820
♪Moonlight westward, the night drags on♪

27
00:01:14,830 --> 00:01:17,920
♪The years have left their scars♪

28
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:21,280
♪Autumn winds sweep leaves;
shadows pair♪

29
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:24,590
♪The past fades like smoke;
tears fall♪

30
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:26,820
♪My heart lies broken♪

31
00:01:26,830 --> 00:01:30,150
♪Lost in thought through endless nights♪

32
00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:34,980
[Love Legend]

33
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:38,780
[Episode 8]

34
00:01:45,510 --> 00:01:46,070
Ruoming.

35
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,480
Lord Pei and Madam Yun will
be here soon.

36
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:49,280
Let's question them first.

37
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,560
You don't know that woman?

38
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,840
No. I really don't.

39
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:56,480
This is your sister?

40
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,350
Where's the rest of your family?

41
00:01:59,550 --> 00:02:00,710
They're all dead.

42
00:02:01,470 --> 00:02:02,840
We've had a hard life.

43
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:06,150
Our father died in the mine
when she was one.

44
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:08,240
Then the mine exploded recently.

45
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:11,800
Our mother and brother both died there.

46
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:15,120
But women aren't allowed there.

47
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:18,080
Mother went as a mine woman.

48
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:20,190
Little girl, what's a mine woman?

49
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:22,630
Enough. Stop asking.

50
00:02:23,630 --> 00:02:26,030
Take them back to Fengyi Bureau.

51
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,190
Please show mercy.

52
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:29,430
My sister is still so young.

53
00:02:29,430 --> 00:02:30,910
I can't leave her alone.

54
00:02:30,910 --> 00:02:31,750
Get up.

55
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:33,630
You'll be safe.

56
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:35,590
We just need you to recall

57
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:36,710
why there was

58
00:02:36,710 --> 00:02:37,870
a woman's head in the basket.

59
00:02:38,310 --> 00:02:39,560
I truly know nothing.

60
00:02:42,150 --> 00:02:43,560
Was it Sister Yan?

61
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:46,430
Sister Yan said someone wanted
to cut off her head

62
00:02:46,430 --> 00:02:48,080
and trade her blood for money.

63
00:02:48,870 --> 00:02:50,080
Trade her blood for money?

64
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:51,470
Pay no mind to a child's words.

65
00:02:51,590 --> 00:02:52,630
She doesn't know anything.

66
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:53,630
She's talking nonsense.

67
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:54,630
All right, Chang'an.

68
00:02:55,730 --> 00:02:57,080
Take these sachets back

69
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:58,390
as evidence.

70
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:06,590
Sir.

71
00:03:06,590 --> 00:03:08,120
These are ordinary sachets.

72
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:09,430
No rare herbs in them.

73
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,400
Anything unusual about the head?

74
00:03:15,750 --> 00:03:16,840
I didn't dare look.

75
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,030
Never mind.

76
00:03:20,870 --> 00:03:22,430
The coroner will examine it.

77
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:25,710
Once you've checked these,
go get some rest.

78
00:03:28,190 --> 00:03:28,800
Sir.

79
00:03:29,430 --> 00:03:30,280
There have been 11 missing-girl cases

80
00:03:30,430 --> 00:03:32,280
in the past month.

81
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:34,590
Aged between 14 and 16.

82
00:03:35,310 --> 00:03:37,080
But the governor won't
release the case files.

83
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:41,120
I recall the governor four years ago

84
00:03:41,710 --> 00:03:43,150
was Yun Zhanpeng.

85
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:45,840
That's right.

86
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:48,560
Back then, he refused
to cooperate with us.

87
00:03:49,150 --> 00:03:50,310
As the Noble Consort's cousin,

88
00:03:50,310 --> 00:03:51,710
he made things hard for us.

89
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:53,240
And the current governor

90
00:03:53,590 --> 00:03:54,870
was promoted by him.

91
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:19,830
It's late.

92
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:21,490
Why aren't you asleep?

93
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:23,390
Sir.

94
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,070
I picked some mint.

95
00:04:25,410 --> 00:04:26,510
I want to make a few sachets

96
00:04:26,510 --> 00:04:27,830
and leave them outside their rooms.

97
00:04:27,830 --> 00:04:28,870
They keep bugs away.

98
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,390
The guys don't need these.

99
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:43,950
Go to bed.

100
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:45,830
I can't sleep.

101
00:04:47,350 --> 00:04:48,560
Close your eyes.

102
00:04:49,410 --> 00:04:50,380
You'll fall asleep.

103
00:04:56,570 --> 00:04:57,160
Sir.

104
00:04:58,240 --> 00:04:59,120
Actually,

105
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:02,480
I have a question for you.

106
00:05:02,950 --> 00:05:03,630
Go ahead.

107
00:05:04,050 --> 00:05:04,920
Today,

108
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:06,920
you mentioned Yun Zhanpeng,

109
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:09,830
is he tied to the missing heads?

110
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:12,000
Has he been sacrificing girls all along?

111
00:05:12,430 --> 00:05:13,870
If it really is him,

112
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:16,040
someone capable must be behind him.

113
00:05:16,830 --> 00:05:17,560
Otherwise,

114
00:05:17,810 --> 00:05:20,270
with his wits, he could not plan it.

115
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:23,270
He would have slipped long ago.

116
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:25,160
That is what I thought too.

117
00:05:27,330 --> 00:05:28,720
I have another hunch.

118
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:31,950
The one who implant the Gu,

119
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:34,910
could it be Yun Zhanpeng
and Zhu Yi's Master?

120
00:05:37,590 --> 00:05:38,360
That person

121
00:05:38,870 --> 00:05:40,310
is of formidable tactics.

122
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:42,310
Anyone who can command them

123
00:05:42,820 --> 00:05:43,950
must be powerful.

124
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,120
I just can't figure it out.

125
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:49,800
Besides the Noble Consort
and the Crown Prince,

126
00:05:50,610 --> 00:05:51,500
who else

127
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:54,400
could make them willingly
do their dirty work?

128
00:05:58,260 --> 00:05:59,480
Could it be

129
00:06:00,010 --> 00:06:02,510
His Majesty won't
let the Crown Prince take the throne?

130
00:06:04,570 --> 00:06:06,110
His Majesty has but one son.

131
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:08,480
Who else would inherit the throne?

132
00:06:10,990 --> 00:06:12,270
I really don't get it.

133
00:06:15,270 --> 00:06:15,680
Don't move.

134
00:06:32,430 --> 00:06:33,240
Lower your head.

135
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,000
Got it.

136
00:06:55,650 --> 00:06:56,920
Sir, I'm going back to my room.

137
00:07:04,780 --> 00:07:07,780
[Prince of Xin'an's Residence]

138
00:07:12,310 --> 00:07:13,800
These were all

139
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:15,390
from girls of matching birth dates.

140
00:07:31,390 --> 00:07:31,920
Try again.

141
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:36,160
Again.

142
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:42,870
Go find more.

143
00:07:43,270 --> 00:07:44,240
If you fail,

144
00:07:45,390 --> 00:07:46,430
you answer with your life.

145
00:07:47,070 --> 00:07:47,870
Yes.

146
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:52,500
[Records Room, Capital Prefecture]

147
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,120
Lord Pei.

148
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:01,270
Forgive me

149
00:08:01,270 --> 00:08:02,510
for not welcoming you sooner.

150
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:04,560
My lord is right here.

151
00:08:04,950 --> 00:08:05,840
Look carefully.

152
00:08:06,310 --> 00:08:07,070
Lord Pei.

153
00:08:07,070 --> 00:08:09,500
[Liu Jinlin, Governor
of the Capital Prefecture]

154
00:08:09,950 --> 00:08:10,920
I need the case files.

155
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:12,480
Lord Pei,

156
00:08:12,750 --> 00:08:14,840
you need an official order
to access the files.

157
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:16,240
The Fengyi Bureau answers

158
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:17,270
only to His Majesty.

159
00:08:17,510 --> 00:08:19,160
Anyone who obstructs us
defies His Majesty.

160
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:20,160
And dies.

161
00:08:21,870 --> 00:08:22,830
I...

162
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:28,630
These eleven young girls

163
00:08:28,630 --> 00:08:30,070
came from different places,

164
00:08:30,830 --> 00:08:31,800
and were different ages.

165
00:08:32,270 --> 00:08:33,670
They did not know one another.

166
00:08:34,550 --> 00:08:36,000
Were they taken by traffickers?

167
00:08:38,550 --> 00:08:41,080
No portrait of last night's victim.

168
00:08:41,780 --> 00:08:44,080
Maybe her family doesn't know yet.

169
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:47,840
She could also be an orphan,

170
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:50,840
or an outsider with no one to report.

171
00:08:51,510 --> 00:08:52,910
This one's only fourteen.

172
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:56,080
Those traffickers are heartless.

173
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:58,600
Sir.

174
00:08:59,270 --> 00:08:59,970
That's strange.

175
00:09:00,670 --> 00:09:02,270
All these girls have birthmarks

176
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:04,080
in the same place.

177
00:09:04,550 --> 00:09:06,030
And they're all the same shape.

178
00:09:08,630 --> 00:09:10,150
Unfortunately, only one body was found.

179
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:11,480
Her neck was severed,

180
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:12,790
so we can't tell if she had it.

181
00:09:13,510 --> 00:09:15,080
Take these portraits back.

182
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:16,480
Have the artists make more copies

183
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:17,550
and post them around the city.

184
00:09:17,550 --> 00:09:18,840
See if anyone comes with leads.

185
00:09:19,230 --> 00:09:20,080
Yes.

186
00:09:24,550 --> 00:09:25,600
There are guards outside.

187
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:26,670
It's safe.

188
00:09:26,670 --> 00:09:27,510
You can take it off.

189
00:09:27,750 --> 00:09:28,440
It's okay, sir.

190
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:29,550
I can take it.

191
00:09:33,670 --> 00:09:34,480
Take it off.

192
00:09:35,090 --> 00:09:35,780
Thank you, sir.

193
00:09:51,910 --> 00:09:52,870
Lord Pei.

194
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:55,240
Lord Pei.

195
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:57,360
I brought you some tea.

196
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:57,840
No need.

197
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,280
Please wait.

198
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,270
We're not picky.

199
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:05,390
If he won't drink it, we will.

200
00:10:05,910 --> 00:10:06,720
Here.

201
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:28,960
Dozing off in broad daylight?

202
00:11:45,650 --> 00:11:46,150
Sir.

203
00:11:46,510 --> 00:11:47,360
What happened to me?

204
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:48,590
You fell asleep.

205
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,200
Where are we going?

206
00:11:52,550 --> 00:11:53,240
Ghost Market.

207
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:55,990
The files show the missing girls

208
00:11:56,130 --> 00:11:58,110
all had ties to the Ghost Market.

209
00:11:58,510 --> 00:11:59,600
Where are Chang'an and the others?

210
00:11:59,890 --> 00:12:01,080
They have other work.

211
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:03,120
You must learn to handle cases alone.

212
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:03,960
Don't always call on him.

213
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:05,630
So you've decided to take me on?

214
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:08,510
Pass the exam first.

215
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:11,840
Sir.

216
00:12:12,030 --> 00:12:13,120
My mask.

217
00:12:13,750 --> 00:12:15,070
It's a private visit. No need for masks.

218
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:27,630
Sir.

219
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:30,870
These masks are so creepy.

220
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:32,550
Of course.

221
00:12:34,270 --> 00:12:35,390
Every one of them

222
00:12:36,270 --> 00:12:38,390
holds the blood of a living person.

223
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:40,200
When I drew the blood,

224
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,480
they were all still alive.

225
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,320
Their cries were music.

226
00:12:43,670 --> 00:12:44,750
What are you saying?

227
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,120
Murder is against the law.

228
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:47,360
It is.

229
00:12:47,630 --> 00:12:49,510
But even if I killed those Wingless,

230
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,390
no one would care.

231
00:12:51,390 --> 00:12:52,600
Who says no one cares?

232
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:53,510
I do.

233
00:12:53,510 --> 00:12:54,720
What a kind heart you have.

234
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:56,030
Lord Pei.

235
00:12:56,340 --> 00:12:57,550
What brings you here?

236
00:12:57,550 --> 00:12:58,750
Proprietor Xiao, have you heard

237
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:00,320
about the missing girls in Ghost Market?

238
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:02,130
I've heard a little.

239
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:03,600
Do you know anything?

240
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:05,440
If you want info,

241
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:06,780
pay a deposit first.

242
00:13:07,750 --> 00:13:08,790
The Fengyi Bureau is investigating.

243
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:10,200
Anyone who hides the truth

244
00:13:10,370 --> 00:13:11,150
gets fifty lashes.

245
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:13,870
Fine.

246
00:13:14,310 --> 00:13:15,550
If I hear anything,

247
00:13:15,850 --> 00:13:17,390
I'll report it to you at once.

248
00:13:18,030 --> 00:13:18,540
Let's go.

249
00:13:20,340 --> 00:13:20,790
Bye.

250
00:13:39,500 --> 00:13:42,540
[Yun Shao, the Yuns' Second Daughter]

251
00:13:44,150 --> 00:13:44,700
Sir.

252
00:13:44,910 --> 00:13:45,550
Your dishes are here.

253
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:47,870
Can you drink?

254
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:49,400
Never tried it. I want a taste.

255
00:13:49,950 --> 00:13:50,910
How old are you?

256
00:13:52,210 --> 00:13:52,910
Eighteen.

257
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:55,630
Still a child. No drinking.

258
00:13:56,150 --> 00:13:58,270
You didn't treat me like one
when you scolded me.

259
00:13:58,480 --> 00:13:59,360
Just one taste.

260
00:13:59,790 --> 00:14:01,510
It's strong. One sip only.

261
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,000
I'm not afraid of strong liquor.

262
00:14:08,030 --> 00:14:09,320
I'm afraid you look down on me.

263
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:20,550
You drink just because I tell you to?

264
00:14:20,630 --> 00:14:21,960
So easily provoked.

265
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:23,240
And you want to pass the selection?

266
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:25,670
If you teach me, I know I can pass.

267
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:26,750
Fine.

268
00:14:27,250 --> 00:14:27,910
I'll teach you.

269
00:14:28,630 --> 00:14:29,320
Listen carefully.

270
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:30,440
I'll only say this once.

271
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:32,960
No matter who you face

272
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,720
or what danger you're in,

273
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:36,600
protect your own life first.

274
00:14:36,790 --> 00:14:37,840
Ignore everyone else.

275
00:14:38,180 --> 00:14:39,600
But you said

276
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:40,440
the Fengyi Guard

277
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:41,980
never abandons those in need.

278
00:14:42,750 --> 00:14:43,270
Did I?

279
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:46,000
Liar.

280
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:48,440
Jerk.

281
00:14:48,790 --> 00:14:50,360
How dare you talk back to your superior?

282
00:14:51,510 --> 00:14:53,200
You lie and insult people.

283
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,080
I didn't insult you.

284
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:56,200
I'm teaching you.

285
00:14:57,710 --> 00:14:58,950
Sir, a toast to you.

286
00:15:09,750 --> 00:15:11,440
You two look unfamiliar.

287
00:15:12,630 --> 00:15:13,910
Don't come here often, do you?

288
00:15:15,150 --> 00:15:16,080
What do you want?

289
00:15:20,030 --> 00:15:21,720
I think I've seen you before.

290
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:27,910
Get lost.

291
00:15:33,390 --> 00:15:33,810
Let's go.

292
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:48,840
Stay behind me.

293
00:15:50,910 --> 00:15:51,720
Sir.

294
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:53,390
No need to dirty your hands.

295
00:15:57,320 --> 00:15:58,390
My eyes.

296
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:02,670
You could've warned me.

297
00:16:03,030 --> 00:16:04,870
I thought you'd dodge it.

298
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:10,270
When did you make this?

299
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:12,270
Remember that peddler

300
00:16:12,270 --> 00:16:13,200
who hurt your eyes last time?

301
00:16:13,550 --> 00:16:14,750
I studied what he used

302
00:16:14,750 --> 00:16:16,030
and made some myself.

303
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:17,840
It's actually very simple.

304
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:19,080
Just different spices

305
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:20,000
and powdered herbs.

306
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:21,550
Should I praise you, then?

307
00:16:21,550 --> 00:16:22,320
Aren't you something?

308
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:23,720
They get hurt,

309
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:24,510
but so do we.

310
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:25,720
Sorry.

311
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:26,960
I'll be more careful next time.

312
00:16:27,270 --> 00:16:28,320
There will be a next time?

313
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,320
Look at my eyes.

314
00:16:29,910 --> 00:16:31,000
Let me wipe them.

315
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:32,200
Sir.

316
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:34,720
Sir.

317
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:35,670
They all confessed.

318
00:16:37,030 --> 00:16:37,840
Bring them here.

319
00:16:38,670 --> 00:16:39,110
Yes.

320
00:16:39,870 --> 00:16:40,440
Get them over.

321
00:16:41,320 --> 00:16:43,080
Mercy, my lord.

322
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:44,030
Please spare us.

323
00:16:44,560 --> 00:16:46,370
That girl and this one

324
00:16:46,370 --> 00:16:48,030
both have a red mark on the neck.

325
00:16:50,830 --> 00:16:52,480
Why did you grab that girl?

326
00:16:52,790 --> 00:16:54,750
She came to Ghost Market

327
00:16:54,910 --> 00:16:56,080
over twenty days ago

328
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:58,080
looking for family.

329
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,200
I kindly gave her directions.

330
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,600
Then she stole my purse

331
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:02,630
and injured one of my eyes.

332
00:17:02,630 --> 00:17:04,030
You must've harassed her.

333
00:17:04,030 --> 00:17:05,460
Why else would she hurt you?

334
00:17:05,540 --> 00:17:06,440
I didn't.

335
00:17:06,540 --> 00:17:08,640
I only tried to touch her.

336
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:09,790
How is that harassment?

337
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:11,680
You scumbag.

338
00:17:12,110 --> 00:17:13,000
Still making excuses?

339
00:17:16,350 --> 00:17:17,270
Where did she come from?

340
00:17:17,270 --> 00:17:18,310
Where was she going?

341
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:19,790
She said

342
00:17:19,790 --> 00:17:21,310
she came looking for her father.

343
00:17:21,860 --> 00:17:23,790
Her father came to Ghost Market
six months ago

344
00:17:23,950 --> 00:17:25,440
and hasn't been heard from since.

345
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:26,960
Right.

346
00:17:27,340 --> 00:17:28,640
Her father was a blood-jade craftsman.

347
00:17:29,030 --> 00:17:29,850
They say

348
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:31,590
he has a rare skill.

349
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:33,110
In Ghost Market,

350
00:17:33,270 --> 00:17:34,680
those who can afford Blood Jade

351
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:36,060
are no ordinary people.

352
00:17:37,150 --> 00:17:38,600
A blood-jade craftsman?

353
00:17:52,210 --> 00:17:55,020
♪A cold blade gleams by the window♪

354
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:59,830
♪Candle tears harden into frost♪

355
00:18:01,150 --> 00:18:02,890
♪Moon shadows flicker and sway♪

356
00:18:03,390 --> 00:18:07,830
♪A wisp of longing haunts the air♪

357
00:18:09,990 --> 00:18:12,660
♪A lone boat rests on the misty river♪

358
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:18,890
♪That promise lies sealed with my sword♪

359
00:18:19,210 --> 00:18:27,240
♪I turn to find the world in snow♪

360
00:18:27,510 --> 00:18:36,130
♪Fated destiny ties from bygone life♪

361
00:18:36,130 --> 00:18:44,800
♪Longing for one beloved flows on♪

362
00:18:45,180 --> 00:18:54,050
♪I can't let go of the verses lost
across this vast land♪

363
00:18:54,480 --> 00:19:02,970
♪Yet I let go of that fleeting light
within your eyes♪
